  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed single-storey side extension, by reason of its size,\r\nscale, bulk, and detailed design, would result in an overly large,\r\ndisproportionate, and poor quality extension that would be out of\r\ncharacter with the architectural design of the original dwelling and\r\nthe wider terrace, particularly when combined with the existing\r\nextensions to the property. The proposal would fail both to\r\nrepresent good design and preserve or enhance the character and\r\nappearance of the conservation area.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposal fails to\r\ncomply with policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character),\r\nLP3 (Designated Heritage Assets), and LP17 (Housing Design) of\r\nthe Hackney Local Plan (2020) and policies D3 ( Optimising\r\ncapacity through the design-led approach ), D4 (Delivering good\r\ndesign), and HC1 ( Heritage conservation and growth ) of the\r\nLondon Plan (2021) and Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and\r\nAlterations SPD (2025).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The single-storey rear extension, by reason of its excessive\r\nsize, bulk, and scale, in combination with the existing side infill\r\nextension, would have a harmful impact on the amenities enjoyed\r\nby the neighbouring residents of no. 36 Forburg Road through a\r\nloss outlook and would result in an increased sense of enclosure\r\nthat would be experienced at the basement level. The proposal,\r\ntherefore, fails to comply with policy D6 (Housing quality and\r\nstandards ) of the London Plan (2021), policy LP2 (Development\r\nand Amenity) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020), and Hackney&#x27;s\r\nResidential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
